questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where order records are unexpectedly committed to the database despite downstream payment failures. In the distributed checkout flow, a `PaymentFailedException` is raised by the external gateway client, but database records created by the service are never rolled back. Here is the relevant service implementation:

java
@Service
public class OrderProcessingService {
    @Autowired
    private OrderRepository orderRepository;
    @Autowired
    private PaymentGatewayClient paymentClient;

    public void processOrder(Order order) {
        try {
            saveAndCharge(order);
        } catch (PaymentFailedException ex) {
            log.error("Payment failed for order: {}", order.getId(), ex);
        }
    }

    @Transactional(rollbackFor = PaymentFailedException.class)
    public void saveAndCharge(Order order) throws PaymentFailedException {
        orderRepository.save(order);
        paymentClient.charge(order.getPaymentDetails());
    }
}
